WEBVTT

00:52.469 --> 00:53.970
Hey there.

00:54.054 --> 00:54.888
Yes, sir?

00:55.555 --> 00:59.350
Why don't you quit standing there
and take a break?

00:59.934 --> 01:02.520
No, not while I'm on duty, Professor.

01:03.021 --> 01:05.315
Protecting you is of utmost importance.

01:05.398 --> 01:07.650
Nothing is going to come after me.

01:08.359 --> 01:10.779
Not on such a peaceful Sunday.

01:10.862 --> 01:15.742
But if something
were to happen to you, Professor...

01:16.326 --> 01:21.456
A few incidents involving
Bora Inquiry Commission members

01:21.539 --> 01:23.208
do not warrant overreacting.

01:24.167 --> 01:28.004
I don't see why anyone
would want to kill me.

01:28.922 --> 01:32.550
More importantly,
I can't enjoy this rare day off

01:32.634 --> 01:34.469
with you stuck to me like glue.

01:35.053 --> 01:36.513
Please forgive me, sir.

01:37.180 --> 01:38.681
Oh, no, never mind.

01:39.182 --> 01:41.851
There's no need for you to apologize.

01:45.814 --> 01:48.149
Do you have a name?

01:48.691 --> 01:53.029
Yes! It is PPB49881327, sir!

01:53.113 --> 01:55.949
I don't mean your registration number.

01:57.534 --> 02:00.120
You have a name, don't you?

02:00.203 --> 02:02.497
Yes. It's Yujiro, sir.

02:02.997 --> 02:06.835
Yujiro. That's a name
that will bring you success.

02:06.918 --> 02:08.002
Sir?

02:08.086 --> 02:10.505
Perhaps you'll become
head of the criminal division.

02:16.761 --> 02:19.139
It's not safe, Professor Ochanomizu!

02:24.269 --> 02:25.478
This is...

02:29.065 --> 02:31.901
A robot dog. Someone abandoned it.

02:31.985 --> 02:34.195
Please step away.
It could be an explosive.

02:37.991 --> 02:39.534
I'm sure it's fine.

02:40.034 --> 02:41.870
It does not seem to be an explosive.

02:44.914 --> 02:46.958
Looks like it's in pretty bad shape.

02:48.042 --> 02:50.461
Let's take this little one
to my home, Yujiro.

02:52.505 --> 02:53.423
Excuse me,

02:53.506 --> 02:56.551
but what are you planning to do
with the robot dog?

02:57.302 --> 02:58.386
Fix it, of course.

02:59.095 --> 02:59.929
Fix it?

03:01.306 --> 03:04.184
I'm the head
of the Ministry of Science, aren't I?

03:12.775 --> 03:15.737
Hang in there. You'll be better soon.

03:18.198 --> 03:20.783
The damage to your actuator
is pretty severe,

03:20.867 --> 03:23.453
but your computerized brain circuits
are the issue.

03:30.418 --> 03:31.544
This is Ochanomizu.

03:31.628 --> 03:34.964
<i>Oh, Professor.
I'm sorry to trouble you on your day off.</i>

03:35.048 --> 03:37.091
It's you again
from the Ministry of Defense.

03:37.175 --> 03:39.469
<i>I apologize for bothering you so often,</i>

03:40.470 --> 03:43.890
<i>but the matter must be discussed
at next week's committee meeting.</i>

03:43.973 --> 03:46.476
<i>To send more troops
to the Kingdom of Persia,</i>

03:46.559 --> 03:50.980
<i>we desperately need your permission
to approve the increase.</i>

03:51.064 --> 03:54.859
No matter how many times you ask,
I will not change my mind!

03:54.943 --> 03:55.777
<i>But, sir--</i>

03:55.860 --> 03:59.197
There can be no more bloodshed,
whether it be human or robot!

03:59.697 --> 04:02.200
<i>But the United States of Thracia's request
is unchanged!</i>

04:02.283 --> 04:03.701
That doesn't matter!

04:03.785 --> 04:07.205
A scientist does not create robots
to be used as weapons!

04:09.165 --> 04:10.166
For crying out loud.

04:13.294 --> 04:14.879
Don't you know when to give up?

04:16.172 --> 04:17.840
<i>What's the matter, Grandpa?</i>

04:17.924 --> 04:21.928
Oh, it's you, Takashi. It's been a while.

04:22.011 --> 04:24.305
<i>If you're busy, I can call back later.</i>

04:24.389 --> 04:27.558
No, it's fine. What did you need?

04:27.642 --> 04:31.646
<i>Well, there was a tornado
offshore earlier.</i>

04:34.023 --> 04:36.025
<i>But now, I'm just playing with Bobby.</i>

04:36.109 --> 04:38.027
Are you two getting along?

04:38.111 --> 04:42.115
<i>You bet! You gave him to me two years ago.</i>

04:42.198 --> 04:44.659
<i>I know there are newer models now,</i>

04:44.742 --> 04:47.537
<i>but he's better than any of them!</i>

04:47.620 --> 04:49.372
<i>He plays with me a lot!</i>

04:49.455 --> 04:50.748
Is that so?

04:51.249 --> 04:53.459
<i>What are you doing now, Grandpa?</i>

04:54.002 --> 04:56.212
I'm fixing a robot dog,

04:56.296 --> 04:58.715
one that's much older than Bobby.

04:58.798 --> 05:02.051
<i>Older than him?
Are you sure you can fix it?</i>

05:02.135 --> 05:03.094
I sure can.

05:03.761 --> 05:05.555
<i>I know you can fix anything, Grandpa.</i>

05:06.180 --> 05:07.974
You can count on it.

05:08.057 --> 05:09.517
<i>Talk to you later, then.</i>

05:09.600 --> 05:10.435
Okay.

05:12.979 --> 05:14.063
Now, then...

05:17.775 --> 05:21.612
I'm looking for a KD-8083 booster

05:21.696 --> 05:25.867
and an RSC-2969 router.

05:25.950 --> 05:27.660
<i>Those are quite outdated.</i>

05:28.369 --> 05:31.164
I've tried several other places, but...

05:31.247 --> 05:34.292
<i>Ah, looks like they're both discontinued.</i>

05:34.375 --> 05:37.045
Any stock at Nakamine Trading?

05:37.128 --> 05:40.256
<i>Unfortunately, no. They're too old.</i>

05:40.340 --> 05:41.507
I see.

05:42.133 --> 05:45.970
<i>The specs for these things
were overhauled four years ago.</i>

05:47.847 --> 05:49.474
<i>What would you like to do?</i>

05:49.557 --> 05:51.976
No, it's okay. Thank you for your help.

05:55.146 --> 05:58.775
I suppose it was us scientists
who changed the specs.

06:01.778 --> 06:04.739
Let's see how much I can do on my own.

06:42.443 --> 06:43.820
I'm sorry.

06:44.320 --> 06:46.781
I was hoping to help you.

06:48.324 --> 06:51.285
You really hung in there.

06:52.328 --> 06:57.458
I know. Your owner
took really good care of you, didn't they?

06:58.459 --> 07:01.754
That's why you lasted as long as you have.

07:02.505 --> 07:04.715
You must have been loved.

07:09.470 --> 07:10.638
Are you

07:12.265 --> 07:14.600
still trying to play with me?

07:18.187 --> 07:19.230
It's all right.

07:19.897 --> 07:21.023
You've done enough.

07:41.669 --> 07:43.796
Who could be here so early in the morning?

07:44.338 --> 07:45.173
<i>Um...</i>

07:45.256 --> 07:47.508
Oh, it's you, Yujiro.

07:47.592 --> 07:49.886
Unfortunately, that robot dog...

07:50.470 --> 07:54.640
<i>A gentleman is here who says
he is the owner of the robot dog.</i>

07:54.724 --> 07:57.185
<i>I'll check his ID
and do a full-body search.</i>

07:57.268 --> 07:59.353
No, there's no need. Show him in.

07:59.437 --> 08:00.938
<i>But</i>, <i>sir...</i>

08:01.022 --> 08:01.981
It's fine.

08:05.943 --> 08:09.197
Thank you so much
for everything you've done.

08:09.697 --> 08:12.074
I'm sorry that I wasn't able to help.

08:12.158 --> 08:13.826
Not at all.

08:14.327 --> 08:17.622
I was looking for him with his GPS,

08:18.122 --> 08:22.126
but I never dreamed he would be seen
by the great Professor Ochanomizu.

08:22.210 --> 08:24.086
Please have some tea.

08:24.170 --> 08:26.005
Oh, no, that's not necessary.

08:26.881 --> 08:29.425
You are a robot too?

08:31.511 --> 08:33.346
Did it make you sad?

08:33.429 --> 08:34.263
What?

08:34.347 --> 08:39.268
When the dog, the robot dog died,
did it make you sad?

08:41.521 --> 08:45.024
Were you sad during the war as well?

08:45.650 --> 08:47.652
Who exactly are you?

08:48.528 --> 08:49.987
Me?

08:50.071 --> 08:52.949
My name is Goji.

08:55.326 --> 08:56.619
Goji?

08:56.702 --> 09:00.331
The one said to have created
the robot army for the Kingdom of Persia?

09:01.415 --> 09:04.252
Your life is in my hands now.

09:05.002 --> 09:06.796
Please summon Atom.

09:06.879 --> 09:08.798
There's someone I want him to fight.

09:09.507 --> 09:12.635
You think I'd summon Atom
because I fear for my life?

09:13.302 --> 09:16.264
You will never force me
to make Atom fight like that!

09:17.098 --> 09:19.850
- I'm not asking you to summon him here.
- What?

09:20.434 --> 09:26.232
You must send Atom to the one location
in Japan where a tornado is occurring.

09:26.941 --> 09:28.401
Hey, Mom!

09:28.985 --> 09:29.944
Check this out.

09:32.154 --> 09:34.782
<i>It's the same location as your grandson.</i>

09:35.700 --> 09:37.743
There's no point in threatening me!

09:37.827 --> 09:42.456
No matter what happens, I will never
let Atom do battle with another robot!

09:43.165 --> 09:45.418
You claim to be Goji, yes?

09:45.501 --> 09:49.130
Does that mean the genius scientist
of the Kingdom of Persia was a robot?

09:50.047 --> 09:52.842
I don't know if I'm a genius or not.

09:53.676 --> 09:57.305
<i>At the very least, I can create
a robot that generates tornadoes.</i>

09:58.431 --> 09:59.265
Bobby?

10:01.309 --> 10:04.937
And one that's extremely lethal.

10:05.021 --> 10:07.273
Robots won't kill humans.

10:08.065 --> 10:08.983
Why?

10:09.066 --> 10:11.527
Because that's how we made them.

10:12.069 --> 10:14.780
In accordance
with Article 13 of the Robot Laws,

10:14.864 --> 10:17.992
we've developed a security system
with multiple layers.

10:18.075 --> 10:20.953
To eliminate
even the most remote possibility.

10:21.787 --> 10:27.793
Wonderful. Professor Ochanomizu,
you truly are a remarkable scientist.

10:28.794 --> 10:32.048
You have developed
so many advanced robots.

10:32.131 --> 10:35.176
And now robots are more human than ever.

10:35.259 --> 10:38.888
What do you think happens
when robots are almost human?

10:39.472 --> 10:42.266
Even then, robots will never kill humans!

10:44.268 --> 10:48.439
What would be
the Japanese word for your attitude?

10:48.522 --> 10:51.525
<i>Seizensetsu,</i> like innate goodness?
Or <i>gizen,</i> meaning hypocrisy?

10:53.569 --> 10:57.156
Shall we test your hypothesis
right here and now?

10:57.239 --> 10:59.241
Whether I will kill you.

11:00.576 --> 11:01.994
Just who are you?

11:04.330 --> 11:05.623
Dr. Goji...

11:05.706 --> 11:11.087
The 39th Central Asian War
started because of rumors about you.

11:11.170 --> 11:14.757
It was said that you built an advanced
robot army in the Kingdom of Persia,

11:14.840 --> 11:19.303
along with robots that could be
weapons of mass destruction.

11:20.054 --> 11:22.014
And who said that exactly?

11:22.098 --> 11:23.974
The United States of Thracia.

11:24.058 --> 11:27.311
Is everything that Thracia says correct?

11:27.395 --> 11:30.064
That's why we formed
the inquiry commission.

11:30.147 --> 11:31.982
And did you find anything?

11:32.066 --> 11:33.442
No.

11:34.276 --> 11:37.238
All we found
was a huge pile of discarded robots.

11:37.321 --> 11:41.200
So despite not finding anything,
the Kingdom of Persia was burned to ashes.

11:42.034 --> 11:43.744
Are you out for revenge?

11:43.828 --> 11:48.916
You're seeking revenge against the former
members of the Bora Inquiry Commission?

11:48.999 --> 11:52.586
Is that why you're trying to destroy Atom

11:52.670 --> 11:55.840
and the other advanced robots
in the world?

11:57.299 --> 11:59.844
See? You've admitted it yourself.

12:01.679 --> 12:04.098
It's possible for robots
to seek revenge, right?

12:09.645 --> 12:10.813
<i>Oh, Grandpa.</i>

12:10.896 --> 12:12.189
<i>Something's weird.</i>

12:12.273 --> 12:14.525
<i>Is there a type of tornado
that doesn't move?</i>

12:16.068 --> 12:19.321
<i>And Bobby's eyes haven't stopped glowing.</i>

12:19.405 --> 12:22.199
Now you have no choice but to call Atom.

12:22.283 --> 12:24.994
You do as Bobby tells you, Takashi.

12:25.077 --> 12:26.537
I'll call you later.

12:29.290 --> 12:30.291
It seems they've come.

12:33.335 --> 12:34.295
The police.

12:35.796 --> 12:37.715
You destroyed Yujiro outside, didn't you?

12:39.258 --> 12:41.135
<i>Squad B, go around to the back!</i>

12:41.761 --> 12:45.848
The police are dispatched
when his transmission stops.

12:45.931 --> 12:47.850
<i>Squad C, get under the veranda!</i>

12:48.559 --> 12:50.436
Professor Ochanomizu,

12:50.519 --> 12:52.313
were you stalling for time?

12:52.396 --> 12:54.732
<i>Squad A has secured the entrance.</i>

13:07.953 --> 13:08.788
Professor!

13:08.871 --> 13:09.997
Oh, Atom!

13:16.003 --> 13:17.171
Wait!

13:17.254 --> 13:18.798
- Wai--
- Let him go, Atom!

13:19.715 --> 13:20.758
Fire!

13:23.302 --> 13:25.471
Go after him! Don't let him get away!

13:25.554 --> 13:27.389
Professor, are you all right?

13:27.473 --> 13:30.559
Never mind that. What are you doing here?

13:30.643 --> 13:34.939
I caught the alarm signal
from Takashi's dog, Bobby.

13:35.564 --> 13:40.027
So I contacted the police
and was told something was happening here.

13:40.110 --> 13:41.654
I see.

13:41.737 --> 13:42.947
Thank goodness.

13:43.030 --> 13:44.740
That's why you came here.

13:45.407 --> 13:48.244
What do you mean "thank goodness"?

13:48.869 --> 13:49.703
It's nothing.

13:49.787 --> 13:51.747
And what's going on with Bobby?

13:51.831 --> 13:53.249
Damn it!

13:56.418 --> 13:57.545
We've found him!

14:04.927 --> 14:06.303
Cockroaches?

14:11.433 --> 14:13.894
They carried something away.

14:13.978 --> 14:15.062
Hey, look at this.

14:16.480 --> 14:18.274
His computerized brain is missing.

14:18.357 --> 14:20.442
Uran did what?

14:21.068 --> 14:23.779
It was after she received
the warning from Bobby.

14:24.613 --> 14:27.741
<i>I tried to stop her,
but she flew off to Takashi's home.</i>

14:30.786 --> 14:33.163
Takashi! We have to go
to the basement now!

14:33.831 --> 14:36.041
Grandpa told you too, didn't he?

14:36.125 --> 14:37.126
Yes.

14:41.171 --> 14:43.465
Okay, Bobby.

14:47.803 --> 14:50.431
What's going on, Professor?

14:51.974 --> 14:55.352
What's happening at Takashi's house?

15:13.037 --> 15:13.871
Fatima!

15:14.622 --> 15:15.789
Fatima!

15:19.126 --> 15:20.085
Fatima!

15:22.588 --> 15:25.883
Fatima! Open your eyes, Fatima!

15:27.176 --> 15:28.135
Fatima.

15:31.347 --> 15:32.556
Where are the kids?

15:33.265 --> 15:34.475
Murat!

15:34.558 --> 15:35.517
Lola!

15:43.984 --> 15:45.235
Murat.

15:48.948 --> 15:50.616
Murat!

16:04.046 --> 16:05.381
Where's Pluto?

16:05.464 --> 16:06.966
His transmission cut off.

16:07.633 --> 16:09.385
So his system overloaded.

16:10.594 --> 16:11.720
That's fine.

16:13.097 --> 16:15.474
Everything's been taken over

16:16.100 --> 16:17.267
by hatred.

16:25.150 --> 16:26.318
Ouch.

16:28.404 --> 16:31.532
Mom! Wake up! Mom?

16:31.615 --> 16:34.868
You can't die, Mom!

16:36.954 --> 16:38.580
What do I do, Bobby?

16:41.542 --> 16:43.961
We gotta go to the basement!

16:45.004 --> 16:47.172
Mom, are you okay? Mom!

16:48.257 --> 16:49.258
Bobby?

16:56.265 --> 16:57.224
Is anyone here?

16:59.101 --> 16:59.977
Bobby?

17:01.186 --> 17:03.939
I'm glad you're safe.
Where's Takashi and his mom?

17:11.405 --> 17:12.865
It's all right now.

17:13.490 --> 17:14.825
See, it's quiet now.

17:15.909 --> 17:18.787
It's like we're in the eye of the storm.

17:20.289 --> 17:21.999
Takashi is in the basement?

17:23.709 --> 17:24.626
Bobby?

17:25.419 --> 17:26.462
What is it?

17:29.673 --> 17:30.883
Any word from the local police?

17:30.966 --> 17:34.094
<i>We can't get through to them.
The signal is too weak!</i>

17:34.178 --> 17:36.513
Please do not worry.

17:36.597 --> 17:38.515
We'll do everything to protect your dau--

17:38.599 --> 17:40.309
Contact Europol!

17:40.392 --> 17:42.603
- Huh?
<i>-</i> I know who's responsible.

17:43.896 --> 17:46.690
The one who's been targeting
the world's most advanced robots

17:46.774 --> 17:48.859
and killing those people.

17:48.942 --> 17:50.486
The real culprit is Goji!

17:51.236 --> 17:52.071
Goji?

17:52.154 --> 17:55.699
He's the man who built the robot army

17:55.783 --> 17:59.661
for the Kingdom of Persia
in the 39th Central Asian War.

17:59.745 --> 18:00.579
It's Dr. Goji.

18:01.205 --> 18:04.124
The designated Europol agent
is Detective Gesicht.

18:04.208 --> 18:05.459
Gesicht?

18:05.542 --> 18:08.504
Patch me in
to Detective Gesicht right now!

18:08.587 --> 18:10.047
I will speak with him directly.

18:10.672 --> 18:13.008
Hurry. If we don't move quickly...

18:16.303 --> 18:17.930
<i>Atom is already on his way!</i>

18:24.895 --> 18:25.771
<i>Uran!</i>

18:27.231 --> 18:28.148
Atom?

18:28.982 --> 18:30.567
<i>I'm headed your way.</i>

18:31.443 --> 18:32.402
Atom!

18:32.486 --> 18:34.113
Your signal's too weak!

18:34.196 --> 18:35.489
<i>I'm almost there.</i>

18:37.241 --> 18:38.075
Atom.

18:39.660 --> 18:41.036
<i>Uran, what...</i>

18:46.250 --> 18:47.584
What was that?

18:49.211 --> 18:51.588
You can have the whole body for 500 ZEUS.

18:52.297 --> 18:53.382
Gesicht?

18:53.924 --> 18:55.008
<i>Atom!</i>

18:55.759 --> 18:57.010
What's wrong, Uran?

18:57.094 --> 18:58.053
<i>...n't come here...</i>

18:58.637 --> 19:00.556
What's wrong, Uran?

19:00.639 --> 19:02.599
<i>No! You have to stay away!</i>

19:06.270 --> 19:08.147
Uran, I'm coming!

19:10.858 --> 19:11.733
No.

19:12.776 --> 19:14.611
Stay away!

19:20.617 --> 19:21.994
Run, Uran!

19:22.077 --> 19:23.829
Atom!

19:23.912 --> 19:26.290
Take Bobby and get down to the basement!

19:26.999 --> 19:29.334
- Okay, but what about--
<i>-</i> Go now!

19:34.590 --> 19:35.465
What is that?

19:39.595 --> 19:41.930
Atom, what is this?

19:42.014 --> 19:43.223
Stand back, Uran!

19:51.398 --> 19:53.025
Atom!

20:21.094 --> 20:21.929
Atom.

20:25.515 --> 20:26.475
Atom!

20:30.187 --> 20:31.146
Atom!

20:33.607 --> 20:35.484
Atom is

20:37.110 --> 20:38.487
dead?

20:50.207 --> 20:51.625
What's wrong, Gesicht?

20:57.381 --> 20:59.758
You had another bad dream?

21:00.425 --> 21:02.052
Yeah.

21:03.512 --> 21:04.805
I'm okay, Helena.

21:05.305 --> 21:06.598
Don't worry.

21:07.474 --> 21:08.308
It's just...

21:10.143 --> 21:12.479
it was different from the usual dream.

21:13.355 --> 21:16.858
You should contact
Professor Hoffman in the morning.

21:17.359 --> 21:19.903
Yeah, I'm sorry to make you worry.

21:20.654 --> 21:22.447
Were you still awake?

21:23.031 --> 21:24.658
Our trip starts tomorrow, you know?

21:25.158 --> 21:27.911
There are a few drawings I need to finish
before we leave.

21:27.995 --> 21:29.454
I see.

21:30.080 --> 21:31.290
You're working hard.

21:31.373 --> 21:33.125
Want me to stay with you for a bit?

21:34.543 --> 21:36.128
Is something wrong?

21:37.045 --> 21:38.922
No, it's nothing.

21:39.423 --> 21:40.590
I'm okay now.

21:50.892 --> 21:51.768
Damn it!

21:52.269 --> 21:53.520
I can't stop shaking.

21:56.064 --> 21:58.233
He's just a robot!

22:02.904 --> 22:03.739
Damn it.

22:04.364 --> 22:07.993
I've tailed him for a while.
There's no mistaking it.

22:08.618 --> 22:11.204
Adolf is trying to kill Gesicht.

22:11.830 --> 22:16.001
That's not good.
We can't let Gesicht die now.

22:16.668 --> 22:19.588
It must be public opinion
that kills Gesicht.

22:19.671 --> 22:20.922
You are correct, sir.

22:22.382 --> 22:24.926
Dispose of Adolf.

22:26.595 --> 22:28.138
I'm sorry, Professor Hoffman.

22:29.014 --> 22:31.350
I know how busy you are.

22:31.433 --> 22:32.351
No worries.

22:32.434 --> 22:35.062
So tell me about the dream
from last night.

22:35.645 --> 22:38.774
Right. It was different
from the usual one.

22:38.857 --> 22:41.151
A new dream, huh?

22:41.651 --> 22:42.819
What was it about?

22:43.320 --> 22:46.615
Well, I'm kind of afraid to revisit it,

22:47.366 --> 22:50.035
so I've placed it in my trash box
and haven't opened it.

22:50.118 --> 22:52.329
I think it's best that you don't open it.

22:52.412 --> 22:53.747
You think so?

22:53.830 --> 22:55.749
There's a chance that it's a virus.

22:57.084 --> 22:58.335
Plus...

23:03.799 --> 23:04.925
Professor?

23:06.343 --> 23:07.177
Oh, uh,

23:07.969 --> 23:11.390
when unpleasant memories come up,

23:11.473 --> 23:14.142
we humans also put them
in our emotional trash cans.

23:14.643 --> 23:16.561
Don't pay too much attention to it.

23:17.687 --> 23:19.898
May I ask you another question, Professor?

23:21.608 --> 23:24.194
There is a human
who's constantly monitoring me.

23:25.320 --> 23:26.571
Monitoring you?

23:26.655 --> 23:30.367
When I'm traveling in my car
or when I'm at home.

23:30.450 --> 23:32.160
Is it some kind of stalker?

23:32.244 --> 23:33.078
I'm not sure.

23:33.662 --> 23:35.497
I'm sure your line of work

23:35.580 --> 23:38.708
will generate all sorts
of emotional reactions from others.

23:41.253 --> 23:46.383
But I highly doubt that this stalker
would follow you to Japan.

23:47.008 --> 23:48.635
You're leaving tonight, aren't you?

23:49.511 --> 23:50.345
Yes.

23:50.929 --> 23:52.764
Relax and enjoy your time.

23:53.265 --> 23:56.226
If this person is still bothering you
after you return,

23:56.309 --> 23:57.686
we'll talk some more.

23:58.186 --> 23:59.312
Until next time.

24:01.731 --> 24:04.067
I'm looking forward
to hearing all about your trip,

24:04.151 --> 24:06.570
like about the science
and technology in Japan.

24:17.706 --> 24:19.749
<i>Director, that doesn’t answer my question!</i>

24:19.833 --> 24:22.752
Did you do something to him?
His artificial intelligence--

24:22.836 --> 24:25.881
We made a huge investment
in Gesicht, you know!

24:28.467 --> 24:31.803
All you need to do
is to maintain him properly.

24:33.513 --> 24:34.764
That's all.

24:47.444 --> 24:48.528
<i>Today, for sure.</i>

24:50.197 --> 24:51.781
<i>I've got to do it today.</i>

24:54.451 --> 24:56.077
<i>Before he goes on his trip.</i>

25:01.791 --> 25:03.752
Change to Route 82.

25:05.545 --> 25:06.880
To my brother's grave.

25:15.180 --> 25:16.056
<i>Brother,</i>

25:17.390 --> 25:19.017
<i>give me strength.</i>

25:20.435 --> 25:22.896
<i>Give this coward the push he needs.</i>

25:32.864 --> 25:34.491
What the...

25:35.575 --> 25:39.955
<i>...passengers, please proceed to gate 68.</i>

25:40.580 --> 25:41.915
How are you feeling?

25:41.998 --> 25:44.918
What? Oh. I'm all better.

25:45.001 --> 25:47.212
Really? That's a relief.

25:47.712 --> 25:50.840
It's our first vacation in a long time.
Let's take it easy and relax.

25:50.924 --> 25:51.883
Yes.

25:52.551 --> 25:53.635
What's wrong?

25:53.718 --> 25:55.595
I'm sorry. It's an emergency call.

25:56.179 --> 25:57.806
Yes, this is Gesicht.

25:58.890 --> 26:00.225
What, an explosion?

26:00.308 --> 26:01.560
<i>Breaking news.</i>

26:01.643 --> 26:02.852
WORLD-FAMOUS ROBOT ATOM IS DEAD

26:02.936 --> 26:04.104
<i>According to the UPB Network,</i>

26:04.187 --> 26:06.523
<i>around 2:00 a.m.
Central European Time last night...</i>

26:06.606 --> 26:09.192
- And what kind of explosive was used?
- Dear...

26:09.693 --> 26:10.735
Gesicht.

26:11.987 --> 26:13.655
Um, excuse me for a moment.

26:15.615 --> 26:18.159
- What's the matter?
- Look at the news.

26:18.243 --> 26:22.622
<i>...the world-famous robot, Atom,
was confirmed dead.</i>

26:23.415 --> 26:24.374
Atom is

26:25.292 --> 26:26.376
dead?

26:26.918 --> 26:29.963
<i>...around 2:00 a.m.
Central European Time last night,</i>

26:30.046 --> 26:32.132
<i>or 10:00 a.m. local time...</i>

26:32.799 --> 26:33.633
Dear?

26:34.593 --> 26:35.510
Was it...

26:36.261 --> 26:38.138
Was it him who did it?

26:38.805 --> 26:39.639
Gesicht!

26:42.851 --> 26:45.604
So he's still alive.

26:46.229 --> 26:47.647
The dream last night!

26:47.731 --> 26:49.024
Atom's time of death!

26:50.150 --> 26:51.818
It wasn't a dream at all?

26:52.319 --> 26:54.279
Unlock the trash box!

26:54.362 --> 26:55.196
Dear...

26:59.576 --> 27:00.702
<i>Gesicht...</i>

27:02.162 --> 27:03.038
<i>Atom!</i>

27:03.121 --> 27:04.456
<i>Gesicht...</i>

27:05.540 --> 27:08.501
<i>You and Pluto are the same.</i>

27:10.754 --> 27:13.673
<i>Are you the one who killed me?</i>

27:15.967 --> 27:18.136
<i>You can have the whole body for 500 ZEUS.</i>

27:19.679 --> 27:20.847
Gesicht!

27:21.806 --> 27:22.891
Gesicht!

27:31.566 --> 27:32.776
There's been an accident!

27:32.859 --> 27:34.402
Someone call an ambulance!

27:36.863 --> 27:37.822
Tobio.

27:39.282 --> 27:40.200
Tobio!

27:46.498 --> 27:48.124
You'll be fine.

27:48.625 --> 27:50.210
Try and walk, Tobio.

27:53.129 --> 27:56.049
Tobio walked!

28:00.053 --> 28:01.012
He walked.

28:02.013 --> 28:03.598
He walked, Gesicht.

28:16.236 --> 28:19.155
The only ones here were children!

28:24.703 --> 28:27.038
<i>- It keeps crashing!
- Artificial neurons are firing!</i>

28:27.122 --> 28:30.458
<i>- There's no virus!
- Scan his memory and prepare to reformat--</i>

28:34.838 --> 28:36.881
<i>Are you all right, Gesicht?</i>

28:36.965 --> 28:39.426
Um, yes.

28:39.509 --> 28:42.637
All functions are back to normal.

28:46.057 --> 28:49.144
Just lie down and rest a little longer.

28:49.227 --> 28:51.938
Gesicht, you collapsed at the airport--

28:52.021 --> 28:53.356
<i>No, I have to go.</i>

28:54.023 --> 28:55.734
<i>Go where?</i>

28:55.817 --> 28:58.153
I'm getting an emergency call
from the station.

29:00.697 --> 29:02.449
I'm so glad you're okay.

29:03.575 --> 29:07.579
I'm sorry, Helena,
that our vacation turned out like this.

29:07.662 --> 29:09.873
It's all right, dear.

29:11.666 --> 29:13.084
I'll be back.

29:20.884 --> 29:23.052
I know you must be worried.

29:23.595 --> 29:26.514
Him going back to work
right after what happened.

29:26.598 --> 29:29.976
No, I'm sure it's better for him
to go back to work

29:30.059 --> 29:33.146
rather than going to Japan,
where Atom died.

29:35.982 --> 29:38.610
I still can't believe that Atom is...

29:40.612 --> 29:42.030
Let me ask you again, Mr. Haas.

29:42.113 --> 29:45.492
You can't recall any reason why someone
might have a grudge against you?

29:46.075 --> 29:49.204
Please stop asking
the same questions over and over!

29:49.287 --> 29:53.291
But your car was blown up on purpose.

29:53.374 --> 29:56.169
It was most definitely
an attempt on your life.

29:56.753 --> 29:58.630
I'm telling you, I have no idea!

29:59.506 --> 30:01.257
And the forensics report?

30:01.341 --> 30:03.676
It was just as we had expected.

30:04.260 --> 30:08.431
We found parts of an MZ-390
from the wreckage of his car.

30:08.932 --> 30:13.603
A compact missile launcher that was
designated as an inhumane weapon.

30:13.686 --> 30:14.813
What's his occupation?

30:15.480 --> 30:17.857
He says he works in import and export.

30:17.941 --> 30:19.275
Maybe an illegal arms dealer?

30:19.359 --> 30:22.737
The bigger concern is who he's related to!

30:22.821 --> 30:25.198
So tell us, Mr. Adolf Haas.

30:26.115 --> 30:28.952
With all due respect, your brother was...

30:30.286 --> 30:32.789
Don't you know
the Blomberg Civil Rights Law?

30:32.872 --> 30:36.793
"Crimes committed by a suspect's relatives
cannot be used in questioning"!

30:37.293 --> 30:38.545
That is illegal to ask me!

30:39.128 --> 30:41.297
As ordered,
we will keep him under surveillance.

30:41.381 --> 30:45.009
But, sir, Adolf Haas's brother was...

30:46.386 --> 30:50.306
A weapon as severe
as the MZ-390 is mixed up in this case.

30:50.390 --> 30:52.141
Do we have any other choice?

30:52.225 --> 30:53.977
Yes, sir.

30:54.060 --> 30:55.687
But at this rate...

30:56.396 --> 30:58.731
Of all people, he's going to be...

30:58.815 --> 31:02.610
The prosecutors are in the dark,
and so are the individuals involved.

31:03.319 --> 31:08.324
There's no problem.
We are the only ones who know.

31:10.410 --> 31:15.039
All right. That will be all for today.

31:27.635 --> 31:30.096
He left for Japan already, damn it.

31:34.851 --> 31:36.644
<i>Received at 8:23 p.m.</i>

31:37.770 --> 31:41.399
<i>You didn't come home
last night either, dear. Are you okay?</i>

31:41.941 --> 31:45.403
<i>I know you're busy with work,
but at least give me a call.</i>

31:48.907 --> 31:50.491
<i>Received at 12:13 p.m.</i>

31:51.200 --> 31:53.995
<i>For reasons you will understand,
I won't be sharing my image.</i>

31:55.496 --> 31:57.957
<i>Adolf, this is a warning.</i>

31:58.041 --> 31:59.375
<i>You are in danger.</i>

32:00.668 --> 32:04.547
<i>Your actions have become
a liability for the organization.</i>

32:06.591 --> 32:09.886
<i>The leader wants you disposed of.</i>

32:11.846 --> 32:12.764
The leader?

32:13.890 --> 32:15.266
He wants to dispose of me?

32:16.017 --> 32:18.436
That bomb today...

32:18.519 --> 32:20.188
<i>Received at 3:45 p.m.</i>

32:22.190 --> 32:23.316
<i>Adolf.</i>

32:24.067 --> 32:25.151
Leader!

32:25.234 --> 32:27.779
<i>I heard you were targeted.</i>

32:27.862 --> 32:30.573
This was right after the explosion.
How did he know?

32:30.657 --> 32:34.535
<i>It's not safe outside.
You should stay put there.</i>

32:35.870 --> 32:38.122
<i>We are all in this together.</i>

32:41.292 --> 32:44.128
There could be another bomb right here!

33:18.871 --> 33:20.665
I am Gesicht from Europol.

33:23.376 --> 33:26.045
I've been assigned
as your personal protection.

33:30.174 --> 33:33.594
Wow! And then what happened
to the bad guy?

33:34.262 --> 33:38.558
Did you get him by shooting a rocket
out of your arm or something?

33:40.143 --> 33:41.019
Dad!

33:41.769 --> 33:44.355
Check this out, Dad! It's so cool.

33:44.439 --> 33:46.691
He's a real super robot detective!

33:47.567 --> 33:49.193
He's so nice too.

33:49.277 --> 33:51.779
I've become a big fan!

33:53.239 --> 33:54.449
Good morning.

33:56.826 --> 33:57.785
Time to go.

33:58.327 --> 33:59.162
Yes.

34:02.331 --> 34:05.084
"A super robot detective"?
Give me a break.

34:05.168 --> 34:07.295
Stop feeding my child stories, all right?

34:07.378 --> 34:09.839
That was not my intention.

34:09.922 --> 34:13.051
So how come
a world-class robot detective like you

34:13.134 --> 34:15.511
was assigned to protect someone like me?

34:16.012 --> 34:19.223
I'm only following orders.

34:19.807 --> 34:21.684
Even if it meant giving up your trip?

34:24.520 --> 34:26.439
How did you know that?

34:28.191 --> 34:30.860
Your boss told me.

34:30.943 --> 34:31.819
Mr. Haas,

34:32.612 --> 34:34.155
do you hate robots?

34:36.407 --> 34:40.578
I'm sorry that you ended up
being protected by a robot like me.

34:47.585 --> 34:49.962
Let me check for any explosives here.

34:57.220 --> 34:59.097
It's all clear. No abnormalities.

34:59.180 --> 35:00.932
Right.

35:02.558 --> 35:04.560
I've checked the entire office.

35:05.269 --> 35:09.315
I'll be in the other room, so please
let me know if you need anything.

35:13.611 --> 35:14.487
Brother.

35:15.071 --> 35:18.157
If only I had the tools to destroy him!

35:18.699 --> 35:20.701
He is so close!

35:22.328 --> 35:23.371
Damn it!

35:26.124 --> 35:29.377
I know that you cops think I'm suspicious.

35:29.877 --> 35:30.753
Mr. Haas...

35:30.837 --> 35:35.258
You think I did something sketchy
to deserve having my car blown up?

35:36.884 --> 35:40.596
You keep saying you're here to protect,
but I know you're here to investigate!

35:42.473 --> 35:44.809
Investigate me all you want.

35:44.892 --> 35:45.810
You don't mind?

35:46.477 --> 35:47.395
No.

35:47.478 --> 35:50.523
But I want you out after you're done.

35:52.900 --> 35:55.987
What do you handle
in your export-import business?

35:56.070 --> 35:57.488
See for yourself.

35:58.656 --> 36:02.368
You mainly handle
computer parts and systems.

36:03.953 --> 36:09.000
You went to Persia
during the 39th Central Asian War.

36:09.625 --> 36:11.169
So what?

36:11.252 --> 36:13.963
Post-war reconstruction
provides opportunities.

36:14.046 --> 36:16.966
Tens of thousands of businesses
took similar steps.

36:17.550 --> 36:23.973
But not many companies can handle
Class A confidential projects like mine.

36:24.515 --> 36:28.227
We are trusted
because of our steady track record.

36:33.232 --> 36:34.150
TV, on.

36:34.692 --> 36:39.530
<i>The body of renowned robotics expert
Ronald Newton-Howard</i>

36:39.614 --> 36:42.825
<i>was found at dawn on the fifth
in a Canberra, Australia suburb.</i>

36:42.909 --> 36:44.202
DR. NEWTON-HOWARD FOUND DEAD

36:44.285 --> 36:46.412
<i>Dr. Howard was known
for his discovery of Photon Energy...</i>

36:46.495 --> 36:48.247
Hey, listen, it's big news.

36:48.331 --> 36:50.917
<i>...murder weapons
were placed on his head like horns...</i>

36:51.000 --> 36:52.543
Hey, they said horns!

36:52.627 --> 36:55.671
I received the report earlier.

36:56.172 --> 37:00.509
Wasn't Dr. Howard the scholar
who made Epsilon?

37:03.221 --> 37:04.680
Don't you have to go?

37:05.223 --> 37:08.476
A scholar who made
one of your friends got murdered.

37:08.559 --> 37:11.187
My mission is right here.

37:14.023 --> 37:15.900
I wonder if Epsilon would even be sad.

37:16.901 --> 37:18.361
I'm sure he would.

37:18.986 --> 37:19.946
He would?

37:20.613 --> 37:21.822
A robot?

37:22.406 --> 37:24.450
Then why don't you go visit him?

37:24.533 --> 37:27.870
Go and comfort him, robot to robot, huh?

37:27.954 --> 37:30.539
My mission is right here.

37:30.623 --> 37:34.043
No matter how you look at it,
it's the same killer as the other cases!

37:34.126 --> 37:36.754
Weren't you the designated agent
on the case?

37:36.837 --> 37:39.507
Ever since then,
there have been several copycat murders.

37:40.216 --> 37:43.594
We don't have conclusive evidence
they were committed by the same person.

37:44.095 --> 37:46.097
Let me show you something interesting.

37:47.932 --> 37:51.102
They mentioned
the Bora Inquiry Commission on TV earlier.

37:52.144 --> 37:54.438
You know of Kara-Tepa Prison, don't you?

37:54.522 --> 37:55.356
Yes.

37:55.940 --> 37:59.860
<i>It's a prison in Persia
run by the United States of Thracia.</i>

38:00.486 --> 38:03.281
<i>My company was contracted
to install all of its systems.</i>

38:03.364 --> 38:05.199
<i>But there was a problem.</i>

38:05.700 --> 38:07.493
<i>Someone tried to erase</i>

38:07.576 --> 38:09.870
<i>surveillance footage
in solitary confinement,</i>

38:09.954 --> 38:11.664
<i>so we were called in for maintenance.</i>

38:12.164 --> 38:14.250
Initially, we thought
it would be an easy fix,

38:14.333 --> 38:16.294
but it turned out to be rather serious.

38:16.794 --> 38:20.089
We ended up having to swap out
some of the hard disk drives.

38:21.507 --> 38:22.425
This is one of them.

38:23.092 --> 38:24.302
Are you not interested?

38:24.802 --> 38:25.636
I am.

38:25.720 --> 38:28.347
What is that? A human voice?

38:28.431 --> 38:30.599
This should clean it up a bit.

38:33.102 --> 38:35.062
<i>Lanke. Tazaki.</i>

38:37.857 --> 38:41.485
<i>Lanke. Tazaki. Howard.</i>

38:42.069 --> 38:43.529
This footage is...

38:44.613 --> 38:45.740
What do you think?

38:45.823 --> 38:48.492
He's repeating people's names, right?

38:49.076 --> 38:52.455
Repeating the names
of the murder victims like a curse.

38:52.997 --> 38:56.375
Perhaps I can enhance it
with my image stabilization function.

38:57.168 --> 38:58.336
Didn't I tell you?

38:58.836 --> 39:03.215
You shouldn't be hanging out here,
protecting me.

39:03.799 --> 39:04.884
Mr. Haas,

39:04.967 --> 39:08.179
you do know what type of place
Kara-Tepa Prison is, don't you?

39:09.013 --> 39:11.891
It's where they keep war criminals, right?

39:11.974 --> 39:12.892
Correct.

39:13.392 --> 39:15.353
The most dangerous ones at that.

39:16.896 --> 39:18.731
Good, it's clearer now.

39:18.814 --> 39:22.943
<i>Tazaki. Howard. Ochanomizu.</i>

39:23.027 --> 39:24.653
Isn't this...

39:24.737 --> 39:27.615
<i>Reinhardt. Lanke.</i>

39:28.699 --> 39:32.661
Mr. Haas! Why did you keep
such important information to yourself?

39:32.745 --> 39:35.206
It's nothing but a video
of some crazy inmate!

39:35.289 --> 39:36.832
How would I know?

39:36.916 --> 39:39.585
- Don't you know who this is?
- Huh?

39:39.668 --> 39:42.463
He's the supreme leader
of the former Kingdom of Persia,

39:43.130 --> 39:45.049
Darius XIV!

39:46.550 --> 39:49.011
He has aged
from the long incarceration, but...

39:49.595 --> 39:52.223
<i>Ochanomizu. Hoffman.</i>

39:52.306 --> 39:53.682
Hoffman?

39:56.644 --> 39:57.853
Coming!

39:58.437 --> 40:01.232
Professor Hoffman is in danger!

40:13.619 --> 40:15.788
My lab!

40:20.501 --> 40:22.878
You're Epsilon!

40:23.462 --> 40:26.507
Professor Hoffman, you're being targeted.

40:27.049 --> 40:28.634
We must get you far from here.

40:28.717 --> 40:32.721
Aren't you supposed to be
a pacifist robot?

40:32.805 --> 40:34.348
This sure is rough treatment.

40:35.808 --> 40:37.852
My creator was murdered.

40:41.021 --> 40:44.942
I'm on the verge of losing control.

40:47.570 --> 40:48.529
So?

40:49.029 --> 40:51.615
Did you get a hold of Professor Hoffman?

40:52.199 --> 40:54.869
No. I'm not sure where he is yet.

40:55.453 --> 40:57.329
I asked for an emergency deployment.

40:57.955 --> 41:00.166
Then why don't you go yourself?

41:00.249 --> 41:02.710
Didn't he help bring you into this world?

41:02.793 --> 41:05.379
I'm more concerned
about the data you have.

41:06.839 --> 41:11.635
There is a possibility
that Darius XIV is involved in this case.

41:12.178 --> 41:15.514
I'll have you submit it
as a crucial piece of evidence.

41:15.598 --> 41:17.641
But...

41:17.725 --> 41:21.479
Could it not be connected
to the attempt on your life as well?

41:22.813 --> 41:23.898
Am I wrong?

41:31.989 --> 41:33.407
Get down!

41:47.838 --> 41:49.340
A Photo-Thermal Smart Bomb.

41:50.174 --> 41:51.383
I've seen that before.

41:51.467 --> 41:55.304
During the Central Asian War,
they instantly vaporized people...

41:56.222 --> 41:57.264
Where did it come from?

41:57.848 --> 42:00.768
Help me! I'll tell you everything!

42:00.851 --> 42:04.980
I'll talk! Just get me
into the witness protection program!

42:06.023 --> 42:11.195
I'm a member
of an anti-robot organization!

42:12.363 --> 42:15.032
That is who's been trying to kill me.

42:15.115 --> 42:16.492
They think I'm a traitor.

42:16.575 --> 42:18.953
An anti-robot organization.

42:19.537 --> 42:22.873
Remember that robot judge
who was killed in an explosion in Berlin?

42:22.957 --> 42:24.792
That was our organization.

42:25.543 --> 42:28.671
What made you become their target?

42:30.172 --> 42:31.590
I promise I'll testify.

42:32.132 --> 42:34.885
So, please, get me
into the witness protection program!

42:34.969 --> 42:38.347
If we don't hurry,
they'll kill my wife and my son!

42:38.931 --> 42:41.433
Please calm down, Mr. Haas.

42:42.017 --> 42:45.813
It seems you're telling the truth.
I'll make arrangements right away.

42:46.689 --> 42:50.276
We'll take your family into protective
custody too. Please rest assured.

42:50.985 --> 42:53.362
Anyhow, we must leave here right away.

42:56.323 --> 42:59.326
Adolf Haas is being protected by Gesicht.

43:00.286 --> 43:02.204
Ironic, isn't it?

43:02.788 --> 43:05.374
But now, it's only a matter of time.

43:05.457 --> 43:09.295
Surely, Adolf will reveal information
about our organization.

43:12.881 --> 43:14.216
Use this.

43:14.967 --> 43:16.093
What is it, sir?

43:16.969 --> 43:20.180
It's the same model that Adolf had.

43:22.683 --> 43:25.311
Death to machines and death to traitors.

43:26.937 --> 43:29.231
The safe house is just ahead.

43:29.815 --> 43:31.650
You'll be safe there.

43:31.734 --> 43:33.402
What about my wife and Hans?

43:33.485 --> 43:36.447
We've secured them.
They're on their way here.

43:39.450 --> 43:40.909
And Professor Hoffman?

43:41.952 --> 43:44.622
We have not been able to locate him yet.

43:50.628 --> 43:54.340
This is no distance to fly
while carrying a living person.

43:55.466 --> 43:57.468
Have some water, Professor.

43:58.302 --> 43:59.345
Thank you.

44:03.015 --> 44:06.185
I needed to bring him this far
for his protection.

44:06.769 --> 44:09.813
You don't want to fight,
so you're leaving him with me, huh?

44:12.399 --> 44:14.943
It's fine. Just what I needed, actually.

44:15.527 --> 44:18.697
With this much bait in one spot,
the enemy will be lured into the open.

44:19.948 --> 44:24.411
I'm not sure how much I can rely
on someone who keeps running away,

44:24.495 --> 44:26.955
even after his creator has been murdered.

44:29.208 --> 44:32.711
Professor Hoffman,
there's something I'd like to ask you.

44:34.004 --> 44:37.966
It's about the secret conference you
and two other scientists had at Kimberley.

44:38.467 --> 44:39.677
Kimberley.

44:40.427 --> 44:41.470
Seven years ago,

44:42.137 --> 44:46.141
you met Dr. Ronald Newton-Howard there.

44:46.225 --> 44:47.559
Oh, yes.

44:48.060 --> 44:53.941
I had always wanted to meet
the inventor of Photon Energy, Dr. Howard.

44:54.525 --> 44:58.112
And there was another scientist
at the conference, correct?

44:59.071 --> 44:59.947
Yes.

45:00.030 --> 45:03.617
A Japanese scientist who invented
the ultimate computerized brain,

45:03.701 --> 45:05.577
<i>Dr. Tenma.</i>

45:05.661 --> 45:08.539
What was the purpose of this conference?

45:08.622 --> 45:12.418
We wanted to share our research
with each other.

45:12.501 --> 45:13.669
"Share"?

45:14.420 --> 45:16.588
Our hope was to create a robot

45:16.672 --> 45:20.551
that could help end wars
and save the planet.

45:21.135 --> 45:23.762
<i>Professor Hoffman,
the inventor of Zeronium,</i>

45:24.263 --> 45:26.390
<i>Dr. Howard,
the discoverer of Photon Energy,</i>

45:26.473 --> 45:30.769
<i>and Dr. Tenma, the leading authority
on computerized brains, gathered together.</i>

45:31.437 --> 45:33.272
What happened at the conference?

45:33.897 --> 45:38.318
Dr. Newton-Howard and I
put all of our cards on the table.

45:39.153 --> 45:40.821
Everything.

45:40.904 --> 45:41.739
However...

45:42.781 --> 45:43.699
However?

45:43.782 --> 45:48.162
Dr. Tenma didn't disclose his research.

45:50.914 --> 45:53.292
This is what he said.

45:53.375 --> 45:55.753
A perfect computerized brain...

45:56.336 --> 46:01.967
a perfect computerized brain will be
capable of suffering, hatred, and error.

46:02.551 --> 46:05.512
Without revealing any of his research,

46:05.596 --> 46:08.932
he understood all of ours in an instant.

46:09.016 --> 46:10.100
He took it and ran?

46:10.184 --> 46:12.770
It's not that simple!

46:13.353 --> 46:17.733
Our research was not at the level
where he could just take it and run.

46:18.442 --> 46:20.778
Yet, he understood it all in a glance.

46:21.403 --> 46:24.615
We humans
call someone like him "a genius."

46:25.991 --> 46:29.620
No, I suppose I should say
he was the one with the perfect brain.

46:31.955 --> 46:35.417
As he was leaving,
he left us with these words.

46:35.918 --> 46:37.836
Let this be a warning to you.

46:37.920 --> 46:39.296
You should be careful.

46:40.672 --> 46:43.801
Stop trying to make robots more human.

46:44.301 --> 46:46.261
Something terrible will happen.

46:47.262 --> 46:49.765
Though, it may already be too late.

46:56.480 --> 46:57.689
Where is he now?

47:00.192 --> 47:03.946
Where is Atom's creator, Dr. Tenma?

47:11.078 --> 47:12.788
Patch me in, please.

47:13.372 --> 47:14.748
<i>Who should I connect you to?</i>

47:15.707 --> 47:17.209
To Dr. Tenma.

47:18.210 --> 47:19.461
Dr. Tenma!

47:20.254 --> 47:24.341
I've been put in charge as your successor
of the Ministry of Science.

47:24.424 --> 47:25.759
My name is Ochanomizu.

47:26.635 --> 47:31.765
It's regretful to see the creator
of the ultimate computerized brain

47:31.849 --> 47:33.392
leave the Ministry of Science.

47:34.309 --> 47:38.605
Computerized brains
are not something you create.

47:40.148 --> 47:41.733
They grow.

47:42.276 --> 47:44.862
Profound sorrow, frustration.

47:44.945 --> 47:47.614
These are the things
that develop computerized brains.

47:48.615 --> 47:50.993
To comply
with Article 13 of the Robot Laws,

47:51.076 --> 47:55.706
robots are equipped with a control device
to suppress their emotions.

47:55.789 --> 47:59.293
This hinders the growth
of their computerized brains.

47:59.376 --> 48:04.756
But, Dr. Tenma, you created Atom,
an absolute masterpiece.

48:06.008 --> 48:07.259
Atom?

48:07.843 --> 48:09.303
A masterpiece?

48:12.055 --> 48:13.682
Atom is...

48:15.726 --> 48:17.519
a failure.

48:22.316 --> 48:23.150
Tenma.

48:23.775 --> 48:26.612
<i>I was unable to find
the line you were looking for.</i>

48:27.362 --> 48:30.115
<i>I was unable to find
the line you were looking for.</i>

48:31.450 --> 48:34.369
Dr. Tenma had withdrawn
from the main stage

48:35.162 --> 48:37.331
and disappeared
into the underbelly of society.

48:40.584 --> 48:43.211
When we set up
the conference at Kimberley,

48:43.295 --> 48:46.214
all we could do was reach out to him
through the Internet,

48:46.298 --> 48:48.008
knowing that he might not respond.

48:48.091 --> 48:51.553
Looking back now,
I'm surprised that he even showed up.

48:52.304 --> 48:56.558
Anyway, he's been missing ever since.

48:57.643 --> 48:59.645
Do you think he came to warn you?

49:01.021 --> 49:03.690
"Stop trying to make robots more human."

49:04.232 --> 49:06.735
"Something terrible will happen."

49:08.445 --> 49:10.197
Do you think he did it?

49:11.448 --> 49:16.620
Do you think Dr. Tenma
actually built his ideal robot?

49:18.121 --> 49:20.624
I think he did.

49:23.085 --> 49:27.297
Detective Lieman, I've confirmed
that Professor Hoffman is safe.

49:28.382 --> 49:29.383
Yes.

49:29.466 --> 49:33.095
I just received word from Hercules.

49:33.887 --> 49:34.972
Yes.

49:35.055 --> 49:36.264
I'm glad that he's safe.

49:36.807 --> 49:37.933
Truly.

49:38.558 --> 49:42.437
And how goes the analysis
of the video data from Mr. Haas?

49:42.521 --> 49:44.690
Hey, let me hear it too!

49:49.152 --> 49:50.445
<i>There's no doubt about it.</i>

49:50.529 --> 49:54.366
<i>It is footage of Darius XIV
at Kara-Tepa Prison.</i>

49:54.950 --> 49:57.452
<i>And the words he keeps repeating</i>

49:57.953 --> 50:00.706
<i>are the names of members
of the Bora Inquiry Commission.</i>

50:00.789 --> 50:03.792
<i>Three of them have already been killed.</i>

50:04.418 --> 50:08.588
<i>But we can't be sure if this is
an actual assassination order.</i>

50:08.672 --> 50:13.802
Did Darius XIV have a grudge against
the Bora Inquiry Commission members?

50:14.302 --> 50:15.137
<i>Yes.</i>

50:15.679 --> 50:19.683
<i>After all, Persia was plunged into war
after the commission pulled out.</i>

50:20.308 --> 50:25.480
But they never found any robots
of mass destruction in Persia, did they?

50:26.148 --> 50:28.817
They found nothing,
yet Persia was attacked?

50:28.900 --> 50:31.194
That must be why Darius hates them.

50:31.945 --> 50:33.530
<i>I wouldn't say they found nothing.</i>

50:34.531 --> 50:36.116
<i>This is classified information,</i>

50:36.199 --> 50:39.202
<i>but included on a list of materials
that the commission found</i>

50:39.786 --> 50:43.165
<i>is a special chip for creating
a highly advanced computerized brain.</i>

50:44.207 --> 50:45.167
<i>Then again,</i>

50:45.250 --> 50:48.920
<i>that does not prove they were
trying to develop a robot weapon.</i>

50:49.463 --> 50:51.131
What is the model of this chip?

50:52.507 --> 50:55.594
<i>Well, let's see.
It's called the Tenma chip.</i>

50:56.178 --> 50:57.387
The Tenma chip.

50:57.471 --> 50:58.555
<i>By the way, Mr. Haas.</i>

50:59.139 --> 51:00.057
Yes?

51:00.140 --> 51:04.770
<i>We're still investigating the anti-robot
organization that is targeting you,</i>

51:04.853 --> 51:08.607
<i>but they may not be
the only ones who want you dead.</i>

51:09.107 --> 51:12.486
<i>You were in possession
of such dangerous data, after all.</i>

51:14.362 --> 51:16.448
<i>We'll ask about the details later.</i>

51:17.115 --> 51:20.660
<i>For now, please head
to the safe house with Gesicht.</i>

51:21.286 --> 51:23.622
How are my wife and son?

51:24.289 --> 51:27.793
<i>They're in our protective custody,
so please rest assured.</i>

51:27.876 --> 51:29.336
<i>I'm counting on you, Gesicht.</i>

51:30.087 --> 51:30.921
Understood.

51:39.763 --> 51:40.972
What's wrong?

51:41.056 --> 51:42.557
I feel nauseous.

51:43.475 --> 51:44.935
Let's take a break.

51:48.188 --> 51:49.898
Let me check if the bathroom's safe--

51:55.320 --> 51:56.863
No sign of weapons.

51:56.947 --> 52:01.952
Inside is just a general-purpose
cleaning robot with no computerized brain.

52:10.043 --> 52:10.877
It's occupied.

52:13.922 --> 52:15.590
I said it's occupied!

52:17.384 --> 52:18.301
What the hell?

52:19.010 --> 52:20.512
Just a cleaning robot.

52:21.012 --> 52:22.347
Message for you.

52:22.430 --> 52:23.306
Huh?

52:23.390 --> 52:26.017
If you want to save your family,

52:27.561 --> 52:29.187
kill Gesicht.

52:31.231 --> 52:35.110
I repeat. If you want to save your family,

52:35.777 --> 52:37.612
kill Gesicht.

52:39.698 --> 52:40.740
Mr. Haas!

52:51.668 --> 52:52.502
Mr. Haas!

52:52.586 --> 52:54.045
You have to stop, Mr. Haas!

53:01.428 --> 53:03.430
I said stop!

53:14.274 --> 53:15.567
There it is.

53:16.651 --> 53:19.821
You've finally shown your true colors.

53:22.365 --> 53:25.493
Did you have the same look
in your eyes back then?

53:26.620 --> 53:27.495
Back then?

53:28.038 --> 53:32.167
Is that how you looked when you did it?

53:32.834 --> 53:34.002
What do you mean?

53:34.502 --> 53:37.130
You're the one

53:37.964 --> 53:39.341
who killed my brother!

53:47.224 --> 53:48.767
<i>He is not a failure!</i>

53:50.268 --> 53:53.939
Atom is a masterpiece,
the pinnacle of human technology!

53:54.022 --> 53:55.857
Professor Ochanomizu.

53:56.524 --> 53:59.903
You don't understand a thing
about computerized brains.

54:01.404 --> 54:04.115
Frustration, intense hatred.

54:04.699 --> 54:08.536
Seething hatred
that could lead one to murder.

54:08.620 --> 54:10.830
These help computerized brains grow.

54:11.414 --> 54:12.707
You're wrong.

54:13.416 --> 54:16.544
Dr. Tenma, you are mistaken!

54:16.628 --> 54:18.672
A brain that is capable of error.

54:19.381 --> 54:21.424
That's what it means to be perfect.

54:22.092 --> 54:25.887
And that is what will give birth to...

54:27.889 --> 54:30.684
the Greatest Robot on Earth.

56:54.202 --> 56:57.872
Subtitle translation by: Astrid Oliver
